sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-06> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Power needed for flight grows as length^3.5 while muscle power grows as length^3 (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "Lift-supported flight with a bounded lift coefficient needs airspeed at least sqrt(2W/(ρ S C_L,max)); under isometry with constant ρ, C_L,max and L/D that minimum speed scales as L^(1/2) and the power required at it as L^(7/2), while power available scales as L^3 only under Thompson's muscle premise, carried as a named hypothesis." ;
    dct:source "On Growth and Form (1917)" ;
    skos:notation "V_{min} \\propto L^{1/2}; W_{flight} = mV^2 \\propto L^{7/2}; W_{muscle} \\propto L^3; per doubling of L: 2^{7/2} : 2^3 \\approx 1.4 : 1" ;
    skos:definition """/-- The `log` form of R5: exponent `7/2`. -/
theorem powerRequired_log {W S : ℝ → ℝ} {k₁ k₂ ρ Cmax LD : ℝ} (hW : CubeLaw W k₁) (hS : AreaLaw S k₂)
    (hρ : 0 < ρ) (hCmax : 0 < Cmax) (hLD : 0 < LD) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁) (h₂ : 0 < L₂) :
    Real.log (powerRequired (W L₂) (vmin ρ Cmax (W L₂) (S L₂)) LD /
      powerRequired (W L₁) (vmin ρ Cmax (W L₁) (S L₁)) LD) = 7 / 2 * Real.log (L₂ / L₁)"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.vmin" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.powerRequired_log", "Delphi.vmin_le", "Delphi.vmin_ratio", "Delphi.vmin_log", "Delphi.powerRequired_ratio", "Delphi.powerAvailable_ratio", "Delphi.powerRatio_eq" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Exact part: lift-supported flight with C_L ≤ C_L,max needs v ≥ v_min = sqrt(2W/(ρ S C_L,max)) (R4, no isometry). Scaling part: under R1, R2, constant ρ, C_L,max and L/D, v_min ∝ L^(1/2) and the power required at v_min ∝ L^(7/2); the power available ∝ L^3 ONLY under Thompson's muscle premise (constant muscle fraction and mass-specific power), carried as a named hypothesis MusclePowerLaw and never asserted. Thompson's momentum-flux derivation is not formalised; the lift equation stands in for it." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-06> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-06> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-06> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.powerRequired_log with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 3 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.5 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean (320 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.powerRequired_log, Delphi.vmin_le, Delphi.vmin_ratio, Delphi.vmin_log, Delphi.powerRequired_ratio, Delphi.powerAvailable_ratio, Delphi.powerRatio_eq: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:00:09.361Z): 3 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [scaling-vmin-hypothesis-dropped] R4 mutant: the hypothesis C_L ≤ C_L,max dropped (replaced by True); then nothing bounds v below and the proof must fail. Rejected with 2 error(s): scaling-vmin-hypothesis-dropped.lean:138:43: error: Application type mismatch: The argument [scaling-power-exponent-three] R5 mutant: power required claimed to scale as L^3 (flight no harder with size). Rejected with 2 error(s): scaling-power-exponent-three.lean:184:12: error: Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern [scaling-power-available-three-and-a-half] R6 mutant: power available claimed to scale as L^3.5 under the muscle premise (then the ratio would be constant and no L* would exist). Rejected with 1 error(s): scaling-power-available-three-and-a-half.lean:202:2: error: Type mismatch Controls: 12 of 12 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

